# xDateR TODO

## "Add to the dated file" button on the Floater panel

Problem: a floater can be dated correctly and still have an error inside it
(ABC110 in the example: the dates are right, but the 1816 ring is duplicated).
The Floater panel cannot fix that. Today the user has to save the dates,
download the dated .rwl with the master appended, load that file as a dated
file, and fix the series on the Edit panel.

Idea: once a floater's dates are saved, a button adds the series to the dated
file in this session, so it can be opened on the Edit panel straight away.

To settle before building:
- The series must not join the master it was dated against until the user
  says so (add it as left out of the master, or ask).
- Reports must stay reproducible: the edit log and the R code in the reports
  need a step that places the floater (the code report_undated_series.rmd
  already prints for a hand-chosen position) before any edits to it.
- Undo / Revert to original: what "original" means for a series that was not
  in the dated file when it was loaded.
- Fix Last Year: a floater is placed by the part that fits, so the default
  may be wrong for it. Say which end to keep, or set it from the lag runs.
- Name clash when the dated file already has a series of that name.
- The Floater guide's last step and floaterFinished text would change to use
  the button instead of download-and-reload.
